      {
        "id": 220344,
        "name": "Roger the Alien",
        "username": "Roger_the_Alien",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/76d3ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-25T04:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello, could somebody please explain me the following situation:</p><p>Guise copied this ongoings from Stuntman:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/LQrIKne\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/LQrIKne</a></p><p>After the environment played a card Stuntman could destroy L‘Embuscade or Guise could destroy Uh, Yeah, I‘m that guy!:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/CTDIfRk\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/CTDIfRk</a></p><p>I decided to destroy&nbsp;<span>Uh, Yeah, I‘m that guy!:&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/fAuwCjb\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/fAuwCjb</a></p><p>My expectation was that the 4 ongoings which were copied would trigger their effects beginning from the first card that entered play till the last card card that entered play:</p><p>1. No time to bleed: Draw a card and use a power</p><p>2. Coute que coute: Draw a card</p><p>3. L‘Embuscade: Deal 5 damage or use a power</p><p>4. Dramatic cliffhanger: Draw a card, play a card, use a power. I may choose the order.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In fact this happened:</p><p>I drew a card:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/CsE0CCc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/CsE0CCc</a>&nbsp;–&gt;&nbsp;<span>2. Coute que coute</span></p><p><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/uEixzgU\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/uEixzgU</a>&nbsp;–&gt;&nbsp;<span>4. Dramatic cliffhanger</span></p><p><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/1jNPhYI\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/1jNPhYI</a>&nbsp;–&gt;&nbsp;<span>3. L‘Embuscade</span></p><p><span>I drew a card and Guise tried to use a power:&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/o1ltIQO\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/o1ltIQO</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/FSQzRBj\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://imgur.com/a/FSQzRBj</a>&nbsp;–&gt;&nbsp;<span>1. No time to bleed</span></p><p>Why was this order chosen?</p><p><span>Although my heroes were at low healt and Gloomweaver at almost 50 health plus he had some cards in play and he was gonna to restore 100 health on his back side... I easily won by the way^^ The combination of this 3 heroes&nbsp;</span><span>really rocked and was pretty fun.</span></p>",
